      "id": 1,
      "text": "Blessing got its name when settlers’ first choice, \"Thank God,\" was rejected by postal officials, so they settled on Blessing instead.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blessing%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1903, Pierce handed the right‑of‑way to the Galveston, Harrisburg and San Antonio Railway, securing Blessing’s future on the tracks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/blessing-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened in Blessing in 1903, with James H. as its first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/blessing-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Between 1903 and 1905, a library building was attached to the train station, serving the growing community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
